# Bounded skill consumer validation

The maintainer authorized execution of the previously proposed solutions on 2026-11-01. Implement isolated local Rust evaluation consumers for the 28 pending technical criteria. Existing product modules remain separate; no marketplace, remote agent, production sandbox or public distribution is adopted. Existing scenario definitions are unchanged.

- REQ-01: Implement replayable bounded consumers for usage, output, context and graph with independent expected results.
- AC-01 → REQ-01: Run all sixteen original scenarios, including negative controls, Unicode, missing prices/providers and bounded cyclic traversal; record each verdict separately.
- REQ-02: Exercise actual process/filesystem/control boundaries in disposable owned fixtures.
- AC-02 → REQ-02: Test four workspace scenarios, streaming cancellation, incompatible/malformed plugin persistence, protected file denial and publication denial after successful verification; unavailable mechanisms remain unverified.
- REQ-03: Exercise Iced scheduling, focus, resizing and hidden-layout counters using a real graphical consumer.
- AC-03 → REQ-03: Record actual graphical heartbeat, focus and extreme-size/hidden-work observations, preserving failures and any remaining gaps.
- REQ-04: Preserve prior evidence and criterion scope; portable exports validate independently.
- AC-04 → REQ-04: Reconcile only affected criteria using current execution and semantic review bindings; preserve previous envelopes and validate SDD/governance and independent export.
